# QLoRA training data and adapter -- fully moved out of the project folder
# to C:\lora_data\lora_training\ and C:\lora_data\sis-qlora-adapter\ (694MB
# adapter + 44MB training data don't belong in a git checkout, and don't
# live here even as junctions anymore). The handful of scripts under
# backend/sample_db/ that read/write them now use that absolute path
# directly instead of a relative "lora_training/...".
*.safetensors
*.pt
base-models/

# The lora dataset-build scripts themselves now live entirely at
# C:\lora_data\sample_db_lora\ -- not even as a junction under
# backend/sample_db/lora/ anymore. Each script's own ROOT-finding was
# rewritten from a relative Path(__file__).absolute().parents[3] (which
# assumed it lived 3 levels under the project root) to a hardcoded
# C:\proj\nic_internship, and the cross-script imports that used to read
# `backend.sample_db.lora.X` now add C:\lora_data\sample_db_lora to
# sys.path and import X directly.

# The remaining lora-pipeline scripts/data that lived directly under
# backend/sample_db/ (not inside the lora/ subfolder) -- same move, as
# NTFS hardlinks instead of junctions since junctions are directory-only.
backend/sample_db/audit_train_grounding.py
backend/sample_db/repair_train_labels.py
backend/sample_db/run_eval_baseline.py
backend/sample_db/eval_set.jsonl

# Local GGUF model cache (multi-GB, exceeds GitHub's limit)
models_cache/

# Exceeds GitHub's 100MB single-file limit
backend/sample_db_new/file_attachment_demo.csv

# Generated by benchmark_ocr_engines.py -- synthetic fixture PNGs are
# regenerated identically from code + font on every run, no need to track.
# The report and raw outputs ARE kept (not ignored): they are the reproducible
# OCR-engine-decision baseline -- see backend/ingest.py's OCR_ENGINE comment.
ocr_fixtures/
